WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:04.567
An agent can act on stale state without realizing its memory is wrong,

2
00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:07.247
so agent memory needs more than storage.

3
00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.807
RAG answers questions about documents,

4
00:00:09.807 --> 00:00:16.067
but a support agent that learns a customer is on the enterprise plan should still bill them that way tomorrow.

5
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.220
To find it again,

6
00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.240
memory is a stack of storage,

7
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.040
retrieval and ranking,

8
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.733
and only what survives ranking reaches the context window.

9
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.973
But perfect recall isn't enough,

10
00:00:26.973 --> 00:00:31.433
since the right facts in the wrong order can make the agent decide worse.

11
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.560
So I'd test whether the agent does better with memory than without,

12
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.940
including updates and contradictions.
